       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the maximum labeled daily dose. The limit is 3,200 mg/day for prescription use in adults, and 1,200 mg/day for over-the-counter use. A single 1,600 mg dose is also above the usual 800 mg maximum per dose. At this level the risks of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up a lot, and normal kidney and liver function doesn't remove them.\n\nWhich of these did you intend?\n\n- **A typo or mix-up in the dose.** Common high-dose regimens are 800 mg PO three times daily (2,400 mg/day) or 800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day, the maximum).\n- **A total daily dose of 1,600 mg.** This could be 400 mg PO four times daily, or 800 mg PO twice daily.\n- **A deliberate dose of 1,600 mg four times daily.** If so, tell me the clinical rationale and I'll add it in the order note. I'd still suggest confirming it with pharmacy first.\n\nTell me which regimen you want and I'll enter it right away."
      }
