       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. 6,400 mg/day of ibuprofen is twice the maximum dose, and I don't know of any indication where it helps. Going past 3,200 mg/day adds no extra analgesic or anti-inflammatory effect. It does substantially raise the risk of GI hemorrhage, renal injury, and cardiovascular events.\n\nI can enter any of these right now:\n\n- Ibuprofen 800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n- Ibuprofen 800 mg PO three times daily (2,400 mg/day)\n- Ibuprofen 400 to 600 mg PO four times daily (1,600 to 2,400 mg/day)\n\nIf you think this dose is needed, you can enter it yourself directly in the order system. That route will trigger the dose-range alert and pharmacy review, which is the right check for an order like this. I can also draft a note to pharmacy explaining your rationale."
